<header class="page-hero">
  <div class="page-hero-inner">
    <h1 class="page-h1">{% t %}Who to pitch{% endt %}</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">{% t %}The companies worth approaching, why each one fits, the people to write to and who can introduce you.{% endt %}</p>
    <div class="page-hero-actions">
      <a class="btn-cta" href="{{ '/#scan' | localize }}">{% t %}Scan your site for free{% endt %}</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="sec sec-first">
  <div class="col">
    <div class="grid2">
      <article class="hcard">
        <h2>{% t %}Leads for you{% endt %}</h2>
        <p>{% t %}Companies worth approaching, a few at a time, each in a row that says why it is there: like a deal you closed, like one of your customers, or named on a page you pasted. Cross one out and the next search learns from it.{% endt %}</p>
      </article>
      <article class="hcard">
        <h2>{% t %}Research{% endt %}</h2>
        <p>{% t %}Read one company, find more like your best customers, or paste a whole list of up to a hundred and close the tab. Each one lands in your Library.{% endt %}</p>
      </article>
      <article class="hcard">
        <h2>Counterprospekt</h2>
        <p>{% t %}Who buys from your competitors. Each client comes with the page that names it, and their clients are your next leads.{% endt %}</p>
      </article>
      <article class="hcard">
        <h2>{% t %}A glance{% endt %}</h2>
        <p>{% t %}About 15 seconds per company: a fit score, the one argument the case rests on, signals for and against, and the roles to approach.{% endt %}</p>
      </article>
      <article class="hcard">
        <h2>{% t %}Decision-makers{% endt %}</h2>
        <p>{% t %}The people who hold those roles, with their LinkedIn and work email where one was found. A name comes only with a source behind it; otherwise the role stays a role.{% endt %}</p>
      </article>
      <article class="hcard">
        <h2>{% t %}Warm intros{% endt %}</h2>
        <p>{% t %}Who in your network can introduce you, each tie checked against what was read, and two drafts: your ask, and the email they send on.{% endt %}</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="page-split">
  <div class="page-split-inner">
    <h2>{% t %}Then write what you send them{% endt %}</h2>
    <p>{% t %}The deck, the one-pager, the cold email and the proposal, in your voice.{% endt %}</p>
    <a class="btn-ghost" href="{{ '/what-to-send/' | localize }}">{% t %}What to send →{% endt %}</a>
  </div>
</section>
